ptic technique"},{"text":"GMP/GLP understanding"},{"text":"SOP documentation skills"},{"text":"Data integrity awareness"},{"text":"Basic QC statistics"},{"text":"Advanced Excel"},{"text":"Basic Python/R for data analysis"},{"text":"3–5 practical biotechnology projects"},{"text":"At least one QC/biotech/pharma internship"},{"text":"Professional laboratory reporting skills"},{"text":"Understanding of deviations, CAPA and OOS concepts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Best Overall Positioning"},{"type":"p","text":"For B.Sc Biotechnology → QC Analyst, the strongest positioning is:"},{"type":"p","text":"Do not become only a laboratory technician. Become a biotechnology QC professional who combines laboratory science, analytical testing, GMP/GLP, quality systems and digital data skills."},{"type":"p","text":"The ideal pathway is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Biotechnology","Laboratory + Analytical Skills","QC Analyst","Senior QC Analyst","QC Specialist/Lead","QC Manager"]},{"type":"p","text":"with GMP, data integrity, LIMS, automation, advanced analytical techniques and AI-assisted quality control providing a strong future-ready advantage."}]}]}